# ================================================================
# ☕ Velvet & Bean Café Management System — Git Ignore Rules
# Layman Explanation:
# The .gitignore file tells Git (our code version control system)
# which files and folders should NEVER be uploaded or tracked.
# This keeps our project lightweight, fast, and secure.
# ================================================================

# 1. DEPENDENCY FOLDER (Massive external packages)
# Layman Explanation:
# The 'node_modules/' folder contains thousands of third-party helper libraries.
# Uploading it to GitHub would waste hundreds of megabytes of space.
# Instead, developers just download 'package.json' and run 'npm install'
# to automatically recreate this folder in seconds.
node_modules/

# 2. PRIVATE ENVIRONMENT CREDENTIALS & SECRETS
# Layman Explanation:
# The '.env' file contains private database passwords, port numbers,
# and secret keys. If this file were pushed to GitHub, hackers could
# see the database password and compromise the café's database!
.env

# 3. DEBUG & ERROR LOGS (Temporary clutter)
# Layman Explanation:
# When npm or yarn encounters an error, it creates temporary log files.
# These logs are only useful on your own machine during troubleshooting
# and should not clutter the shared codebase.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# 4. OPERATING SYSTEM ARTIFACTS
# Layman Explanation:
# macOS Finder (.DS_Store) and Windows Explorer (Thumbs.db) automatically
# create hidden preview files for folder icon positions and thumbnails.
# These have nothing to do with programming and are safely ignored.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

